      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Name clash: sold as B. semperflorens-cultorum; tuberous begonia (B. x tuberhybrida) and rex begonias are separate entries. Watering: RHS says water regularly during dry periods but avoid wetting the foliage; profile says moist but well-drained, neutral to slightly acid soil in partial shade. NC State has no page under these names (both URLs 404), so the second source for watering is the RHS profile. let_top_dry is the agent's mapping; 3 days is a guess. Light: partial shade (both RHS pages; foliage may scorch in hot sun). Size: RHS 15 to 50 cm height and spread, 30 by 30 is the agent's middle. Habit bushy: RHS profile. Hardiness: tender perennial grown as an annual (RHS), H1C. Toxicity: ASPCA lists the genus Begonia spp. as toxic to dogs, cats and horses, soluble calcium oxalates, vomiting and salivation, most toxic part underground; severity 1 is our grading (mild GI signs in dogs and cats); genus-level, not B. cucullata specifically. The RHS profile's pets line is generic bulb wording and was not used. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
